.\" Man page for proteus(1)
.TH PROTEUS 1 "2026-05-06" "0.1.0" "Proteus Manual"
.SH NAME
proteus \- erase network-layer fingerprints on Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B proteus
[\fIglobal-options\fR]
.I subcommand
[\fIsubcommand-options\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B proteus
is a Rust CLI for Linux that erases the network identifiers your laptop hands
out every time it joins a network: MAC addresses, DHCP options, IPv6
derivations, hostname, mDNS chatter, TCP fingerprint quirks, and Bluetooth
adapter alias. It rotates MACs on a schedule (default 2h) and on probe-driven
connectivity loss (default every 5m). It ships as a single binary with an
embedded wiki and targets Fedora 43+ with systemd and NetworkManager.
.PP
There is no daemon. The CLI is the whole product. Two systemd timers
(\fBproteus-rotate.timer\fR at 2h, \fBproteus-check.timer\fR at 5m) and a boot
oneshot call back into the binary; everything else is on-demand. State lives
in \fI/var/lib/proteus/state.json\fR and config in
\fI/etc/proteus/config.toml\fR. The first time Proteus sees a system it caches
the permanent MAC and original hostname; those are sacred and never
re-captured. Anything Proteus writes under \fI/etc/\fR carries a
managed-by-proteus header plus a SHA of the expected content so drift is
detectable.
.PP
Proteus is a network-layer fingerprint eraser, not a privacy suite. It does
not touch TLS or browser fingerprints, DNS resolution policy beyond stripping
EDNS Client Subnet, tracker blocking, or traffic correlation. It refuses to
weaken Fedora's crypto-policies, touch \fI/etc/ssh/ssh_config\fR, or rotate
\fI/etc/machine-id\fR. Mutating commands need root; read commands work for
any user and degrade quietly when files are not readable.
.SH OPTIONS
The flags below are global \(em they apply to every subcommand and must
precede the subcommand name. Per-subcommand flags are listed under
\fBSUBCOMMANDS\fR below.
.IP "\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR" 4
Increase log verbosity. Repeatable: \fB\-v\fR debug, \fB\-vv\fR trace.
.IP "\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR" 4
Decrease log verbosity. Repeatable: \fB\-q\fR warn, \fB\-qq\fR error.
.IP "\fB\-\-config\fR \fIPATH\fR" 4
Override the default config path \fI/etc/proteus/config.toml\fR. Useful for
testing.
.IP "\fB\-\-state\fR \fIPATH\fR" 4
Override the default state path \fI/var/lib/proteus/state.json\fR. Useful for
testing.
.IP "\fB\-\-no\-color\fR" 4
Disable ANSI colors on stderr log output. Honors \fBNO_COLOR\fR too.
.IP "\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR" 4
Print help and exit 0.
.IP "\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR" 4
Print version and exit 0.
.PP
\fBRUST_LOG\fR overrides \fB\-v\fR / \fB\-q\fR when set; see
\fBENVIRONMENT\fR below.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
Mutating commands require root and accept \fB\-\-yes\fR for non-interactive
runs. Read commands degrade quietly when files are not readable.
.SS apply
.B proteus apply
[\fB\-\-yes\fR]
.PP
Apply the current config to the system: rotate MACs that need rotating, write
managed files under \fI/etc/\fR, install systemd timers. Idempotent. Mutating;
requires root. See \fBproteus wiki concepts\fR.
.SS current
.B proteus current
[\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-iface\fR \fINAME\fR]
.PP
Show the current network identifiers your system is handing out right now.
Read-only. \fB\-\-iface\fR limits to one interface. See \fBproteus wiki
mac-recipes\fR.
.SS diff
.B proteus diff
[\fB\-\-json\fR]
.PP
Show the delta between current config, built-in defaults, and live system
state. Flags drift from managed files via the SHA in their header. Read-only.
.SS dry-run
.B proteus dry-run
.I subcommand
[\fIargs\fR...]
.PP
Preview the mutations a command would make without performing them. Every
mutator goes through a Plan enum that can be either previewed or executed.
Read-only.
.SS help
.B proteus help
[\fIfeature\fR]
.PP
Friendly entry point. With no argument, lists embedded wiki pages. With a
feature name, prints the matching wiki page. Effectively an alias for
\fBwiki\fR \fIfeature\fR with a friendlier zero-arg behavior. Note:
\fBproteus help\fR is not the same as \fBproteus \-\-help\fR. The latter is
the clap usage; the former opens the wiki.
.SS original
.B proteus original
[\fB\-\-json\fR]
.PP
Show the cached original MACs and hostname Proteus snapshotted on first run.
Sacred \(em never re-captured. State path defaults to
\fI/var/lib/proteus/state.json\fR; override with \fB\-\-state\fR. Read-only.
The cache populates the first time a mutating command runs.
.SS pin
.B proteus pin
.I target
.PP
Pin a MAC to a specific interface or NetworkManager connection. Pinned
targets are skipped by both scheduled and probe-driven rotation. \fItarget\fR
is an interface name or NM connection profile (profile preferred when
ambiguous). Mutating; requires root. See \fBproteus wiki mac-recipes\fR.
.SS reset
.B proteus reset
[\fB\-\-yes\fR]
.PP
Clear \fI/etc/proteus/config.toml\fR to defaults and re-apply. The "I
tinkered and broke it" hatch. Deliberately does not touch the cached original
MACs in \fIstate.json\fR \(em those remain sacred. Mutating; requires root.
.SS revert
.B proteus revert
[\fB\-\-yes\fR]
.PP
Restore everything to the cached originals. The panic button. Invariant: must
work at every commit \(em if a feature cannot be backed out cleanly, it does
not ship. Mutating; requires root.
.SS rotate
.B proteus rotate
[\fB\-\-iface\fR \fINAME\fR] [\fB\-\-yes\fR]
.PP
Generate a fresh MAC and apply it. With no \fB\-\-iface\fR, rotates every
managed interface. Skips pinned interfaces. Avoids picking a MAC that matches
the gateway or anything else in the local ARP table. Mutating; requires root.
See \fBproteus wiki mac-recipes\fR.
.SS show-config
.B proteus show-config
[\fB\-\-json\fR]
.PP
Print the active config from \fI/etc/proteus/config.toml\fR (override with
\fB\-\-config\fR). When the file is missing, prints a note that defaults are
in effect and exits 0. Read-only. See \fBproteus wiki config\fR.
.SS show-defaults
.B proteus show-defaults
[\fB\-\-json\fR]
.PP
Print the built-in default config. Use this to see every knob and its default
before writing your own \fIconfig.toml\fR. Read-only; never touches the
filesystem.
.SS status
.B proteus status
[\fB\-\-json\fR]
.PP
The overall system + per-feature status report: whether systemd,
NetworkManager, BlueZ, and systemd-resolved are present; physical interfaces
with their current MAC; per-feature \fBapplied\fR / \fBskipped\fR (reason) /
\fBfailed\fR (reason). Read-only.
.SS uninstall
.B proteus uninstall
[\fB\-\-purge\fR] [\fB\-\-yes\fR]
.PP
Full removal. Runs \fBrevert\fR first, removes the binary, removes the
systemd timers. With \fB\-\-purge\fR, also deletes \fI/etc/proteus/\fR and
\fI/var/lib/proteus/\fR. Without \fB\-\-purge\fR the original-MAC cache is
preserved so a reinstall can restore the same identity. Mutating; requires
root. See \fBproteus wiki uninstall\fR.
.SS unpin
.B proteus unpin
.I target
.PP
Remove a pin previously set with \fBpin\fR. The target rejoins the rotation
pool. \fItarget\fR is an interface name or NM connection profile. Mutating;
requires root.
.SS wiki
.B proteus wiki
[\fIpage\fR]
.PP
Browse the embedded wiki. With no argument, lists available pages. With a
page name, prints that page's Markdown to stdout. Read-only.
.SH EXIT CODES
Stable. New codes may be added in future versions; existing codes never
change meaning. Defined in \fBsrc/lib.rs\fR (\fBexit::*\fR).
.IP "\fB0\fR" 6
\fBSUCCESS\fR \(em success.
.IP "\fB1\fR" 6
\fBGENERIC_ERROR\fR \(em generic / unclassified error.
.IP "\fB2\fR" 6
Reserved for clap's invalid-arguments default (usage error from the parser).
.IP "\fB64\fR" 6
\fBNOT_IMPLEMENTED\fR \(em command parses but the selected backend / driver
path does not drive this feature; stderr names what is missing.
.IP "\fB65\fR" 6
\fBCONFIG_ERROR\fR \(em config parse failure or invalid value. Also returned
as \fBCONFIRMATION_REQUIRED\fR when a mutating command is invoked without
\fB\-\-yes\fR.
.IP "\fB66\fR" 6
\fBPERMISSION_ERROR\fR \(em mutating command run without root, or read denied
on a privileged file.
.IP "\fB70\fR" 6
\fBSYSTEM_NOT_SUPPORTED\fR \(em not Linux, no systemd, or another
precondition the binary cannot satisfy.
.IP "\fB75\fR" 6
\fBLOCK_BUSY\fR \(em another \fBproteus\fR instance is holding the state
lock; safe to retry. Raise \fBPROTEUS_LOCK_TIMEOUT_MS\fR if persistent.
.PP
Wrappers should treat 0 as success and any non-zero as failure. Inspect
stderr or journald for the human reason; do not scrape stdout for status \(em
\fB\-\-json\fR is the contract.
.SH FILES
.IP "\fI/etc/proteus/config.toml\fR" 4
Config file. Override with \fB\-\-config\fR. When absent, built-in defaults
apply.
.IP "\fI/var/lib/proteus/state.json\fR" 4
Captured originals (permanent MACs, original hostname) plus managed state.
The original-MAC cache is sacred \(em populated on first run, never
re-captured. Override with \fB\-\-state\fR.
.IP "\fI/etc/sysctl.d/95\-proteus.conf\fR" 4
Sysctl drop-in for stack-fingerprint hardening (TCP timestamps off, ICMP
info-reply drops, ARP suppression).
.IP "\fI/etc/systemd/resolved.conf.d/10\-proteus\-*.conf\fR" 4
systemd-resolved drop-ins for the ECS-strip knob and discovery-silencing
(mDNS responder/resolver, LLMNR).
.IP "\fI/etc/systemd/system/proteus\-*.{timer,service}\fR" 4
systemd timer and service units that schedule rotation
(\fBproteus-rotate.timer\fR at 2h), connectivity probes
(\fBproteus-check.timer\fR at 5m), and the boot oneshot
(\fBproteus-boot.service\fR).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.IP "\fBRUST_LOG\fR" 4
Standard \fBtracing\fR filter syntax. Overrides \fB\-v\fR / \fB\-q\fR when
set. Examples: \fBRUST_LOG=debug\fR, \fBRUST_LOG=proteus=trace\fR.
.IP "\fBNO_COLOR\fR" 4
When set to any value, disables ANSI colors on stderr log output. Same as
\fB\-\-no\-color\fR.
.IP "\fBJOURNAL_STREAM\fR" 4
Set by systemd when running under a unit. When present, Proteus routes log
output to journald via \fBtracing-journald\fR; otherwise it falls back to
stderr.
.SH EXAMPLES
Read overall system + per-feature state:
.PP
.RS 4
.B proteus status
.RE
.PP
Machine-readable status (pipe through \fBjq\fR(1) for filtering):
.PP
.RS 4
.B proteus status \-\-json | jq .interfaces
.RE
.PP
Rotate the MAC for a single Wi-Fi interface:
.PP
.RS 4
.B sudo proteus rotate \-\-iface wlan0
.RE
.PP
Apply the current config to the system:
.PP
.RS 4
.B sudo proteus apply \-\-yes
.RE
.PP
Restore everything to the cached originals:
.PP
.RS 4
.B sudo proteus revert \-\-yes
.RE
.PP
Read the concepts page from the embedded wiki:
.PP
.RS 4
.B proteus wiki concepts
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nmcli (1),
.BR bluetoothctl (1),
.BR tcpdump (1),
.BR systemd-resolved.service (8),
.BR NetworkManager (8)
.PP
The full embedded wiki is browsable via \fBproteus wiki\fR. Key pages:
\fBintro\fR, \fBquickstart\fR, \fBconcepts\fR, \fBcli\fR, \fBconfig\fR,
\fBmac-recipes\fR, \fBcaptive-portals\fR, \fBdns\fR, \fBthreat-model\fR,
\fBtroubleshooting\fR, \fBverifying\fR, \fBuninstall\fR.
